title: Revision commands in the GUI
tags: [[Event log]]
kind: guide
summary: Undo, redo, revert, rollback, label and prune from the GUI — confirmations before, files carried along, no questions while the repository is locked.

* <<key "log:undo" Ctrl+z>> / <<key "log:redo" Ctrl+Shift+z>> — from anywhere: the same selection as `mf log undo`/`redo` ([[Undo and redo]]). Neither asks — the result is itself undoable. A revert undo picks that is ''blocked'' is reported, naming `log:revert with-dependents`, rather than pulling someone else's changes in behind your back.
* <<key "log:revert" Shift+r>> — reverts what the log panel has selected: the revision, or the single operation under the cursor ("undo just this one field" in one key). A confirmation names how many operations it undoes, says when files will move, and warns when the target was already undone. <<key "log:revert op" Shift+o>> narrows from a revision row (asking which operation when there are several), <<key "log:revert revision" Shift+v>> widens back.
* <<key "log:revert with-dependents" Shift+d>> — the same on the dependency closure, always confirmed with how many operations it pulled in ([[Operation dependencies]]). A ''blocked'' plain revert does not open the dialog: the panel selects the blocking revision and says which operation stands in the way — "revert that one first" is then one key away — and offers this wider revert as the other way out.
* `log:rollback` — after a confirmation, moves HEAD to the last operation of the selected revision: back, or forward and onto another branch — which is also how a rollback is undone ([[Rollback]]).
* <<key "log:mark" Shift+l>> — sets or clears the selected revision's label.
* `log:prune` — after a confirmation, prunes everything before the selected revision, for good ([[Pruning the log]]). Keeping the last N revisions, or linearizing, is `mf log prune`.

''Files are carried with the metadata.'' Every navigation and revert the GUI writes goes
through the same code as the CLI (`core::navigation`): one atomic request when no step
touches a file, otherwise the coordinated form — moving a file back, bringing content back
from the trash, sending it back there ([[Filesystem coordination]]). Every confirmation
comes ''before'' the repository is locked, and nothing asks while it is: a move is applied
whether or not the file is where the log says (when it is not, the metadata keeps the
recorded path). What the file actions had to report follows the summary in the status bar.
The panels refresh afterwards.
